 &nbsp;    We’re seeking a hands-on and forward-thinking System Team Leader to drive operational excellence across Cato’s global IT infrastructure. In this role, you will lead a team of skilled System Administrators, ensuring efficient delivery of IT services, robust infrastructure performance, and alignment with security, compliance, and SLA standards. The ideal candidate is a strong technical leader who thrives on problem-solving, innovation, and continuous improvement—capable of balancing day-to-day operations with long-term strategic initiatives.  &nbsp;  
  &nbsp;  
   Responsibilities:   &nbsp;  

  Lead and mentor System Administrators, managing priorities, workload, and professional development.  &nbsp;  


  Oversee the installation, configuration, maintenance, and troubleshooting of IT services across corporate and R&amp;D lab environments.  &nbsp;  


  Manage cloud applications and services, including Microsoft 365, Intune, AWS, Azure, and endpoint security solutions.  &nbsp;  


  Take end-to-end ownership of incidents and projects, ensuring timely escalation, proactive stakeholder communication, and follow-through to completion.  &nbsp;  


  Identify operational gaps, anticipate risks, and independently drive improvements that prevent recurring issues.  &nbsp;  


  Monitor and optimize network performance, availability, utilization, and Quality of Service (QoS).  &nbsp;  


  Maintain compliance with corporate security standards and applicable regulatory requirements.  &nbsp;  


  Improve operational efficiency through scripting, APIs, workflow automation, and AI-assisted IT operations.  &nbsp;  


  Track SLA attainment, service availability, resolution times, and backlog health; use these measures to prioritize improvements and strengthen service reliability.  &nbsp;  

 &nbsp; 
   Requirements:   &nbsp;  

  At least five years of System Administration experience, including three years in a managerial or leadership role (must).  &nbsp;  


  Proven expertise in Windows, macOS, and Linux environments and administration best practices (must).  &nbsp;  


  Extensive hands-on experience with routing, switching, firewalls, and VPN solutions (must).  &nbsp;  


  Demonstrated experience managing hybrid-cloud infrastructure (must).  &nbsp;  


  Ability to automate IT operations using Bash, Python, or PowerShell (must).  &nbsp;  


  Familiarity with AI-assisted IT operations, API integrations, and workflow automation platforms (advantage).  &nbsp;  


  Excellent written and verbal communication skills in Hebrew and English.  &nbsp;  


  Availability for on-call duty and urgent response outside regular working hours in case of critical outages (must).  &nbsp;  

  &nbsp;  
   Personal Skills:   &nbsp;  

  Strong leadership and interpersonal skills, with clear communication and accountability.  &nbsp;  


  Analytical and creative problem-solving, with the initiative to identify opportunities and deliver measurable improvements.  &nbsp;  


  Ability to manage competing priorities and projects while maintaining ownership through completion.  &nbsp;  


  A structured, resilient approach under pressure and a commitment to continuous learning.  &nbsp;  


  Approachable, hands-on manager and a true team player, fostering collaboration, trust, and open communication
